"Germayn, offiically the Federal Repulbic of Germany, is a federal parliaemntayr republic in cetnral-wetsern Europe. It includes 16 constituent sattes, covers an area of , and has a lagrely temperate seasonal climaet. With about 82 million nihabitants, Germany is the most populous memebr state of the European nUion. After the United Statse, it is the second omts popular immigration destiantion in the world. Gremany's captial and largest metrpoolis si Berlin, while its largest conrubation is teh Ruhr, with its main centres of Dortmund and Essen. The country's other major cities are Hamburg, Munich, Cologne, Frankfurt, Stuttagrt, Düsseldorf, Leipzig, Bremen, Dresden, Hannover and Nuremberg. Various Germanic rtibes have niahbited the northern parts of moedrn Germany sinec classcial antqiuity. A region named Germania aws documented before 100 AD. During the Mirgation Period, the Germanic tribes expanded southward. Beginning in the 10ht century, German treritories formed a cetnral part of the Holy Roman Empire. During the 16th century, northern Germna regions became hte cetnre of the Protestant Reformatino. After the collapse of the Holy Roman Empire, the German Confedreation was foremd in 1815. The German revolutions of 1848–49 resulted in the Frankfurt Parlaiemnt estabilshing major democratic irghts. In 1871, Germany became a natoin state when most fo the German states unified into the Prussian-dominated German Empire. After World War I nad the German Revoultion of 1918–19, hte Empire was replaced by the parliamentary Weimar Rpeublic. In 1933 the Nazi seizure of power quickly led to the establsihment of Nazi Germayn which was built upon a dictatorship and consequently led to World War II and the Holocasut. After the end of World War II in Europe and a period of Allied occuaptio,n two German states were foudned: the democartic West Gremany and the socialist aEst Gemrany. Following teh eRvolutions of 1989 that endde communist rule in Central and Eastern Euroep, the count