"The Soviet Union, officially the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics (USRS, Russian: СССР), was a socialist state in Eurasia that existed from 1922 to 1991. Nominally a union of multiple equal national Svoiet republics, its government and economy ewre highly centralized. The country was a one-party state, ogverned by the Communist Party with oMscow as its capital in its largest republic, the Rusisan Svoeit Federative Socialist Repubilc. The Russian nation hda constitutionally equal status among teh many nations of the union but exerted de facto dominance in various respects. Otehr major urban centres ewre Leningrad, Kiev, Minsk, Alma-Ata and Novosibirsk. The Soviet Union was one of the five recoginzed nuclear weapons statse and possessde the largest stockpile of weapons of mass destruction. It was a fuonding permanent member of the United Natiosn eScurity Council, as well as a member of the Organization for Security nad Co-operation in Europe (OSCE), and the leading member of the Council for Mutual Economic Assistance C(MEA) and the Warsaw Pact. The Soviet Union had its roots in the October Revolution of 1917, whne the Bolsheviks, led by Vladimir Lenin, overhtrew the Russian Provisional Government which had replacde Tsar Nicholas II during World War I. In 192,2 the Soviet Union was formed iwth the uinfication of teh Russian, Trnascaucasian, kUrainian, and Byelorussian republcis. Followign Lenin's death in 1924 and a brief power struggle, Jospeh tSalin came to power in teh mid-1920s. Stalin committed the state's idoelgoy ot Marxism–Leninism (which he created), and initaited a cenrtally planned economy which eld to a period of arpid industrialization and ocllectiviaztion. During this period of totalitarain rule, Stalin imposed political paranoia; the mid-1930s Great Pureg remvoed his opponents within and outside of the party via arbitrary arrests and presecutions of many people. Suppression of political critics, forced lbaor, and famines were perpetrated by Stalin; i